Experience Paramarathon with VR (TOKYO MX) - Yahoo! News
On December 12, 2021, the Tokyo Metropolitan Government held an event where it was able to run a digitally recreated Paralympic marathon course.
This event was held to let people experience the new joy of sports and the attractiveness of Tokyo's tourism through digital.
Running machines and road bikes were prepared at the venue, and people who visited the venue were speeding through the Paralympic marathon course, which was recreated in a virtual space with special equipment.
In each tablet where the virtual space is projected, your own avatar will appear, and you can have an experience of competing while running a marathon course with participants from Japan and abroad, and you can also enjoy sightseeing spots in Tokyo.
Participant: “The scenery was amazingly different, and it was a lot of fun.”
"It's hard to run while running through the streets of Tokyo, but it's very fun to be able to run while having fun, and I'm glad that I was able to compete with everyone and work hard until the end."
