Posco International Acquires Senex Energy in Australia, Expands Overseas Gasfield Business (WoW!Korea) - Yahoo! News
Posco International said on Tuesday that it had entered into a share acquisition agreement for Senex Energy in Australia, as well as an investment agreement with Hancock Energy to acquire Senex Energy.
Currently, procedures such as the approval at Senex Energy’s general meeting of shareholders and the approval of the local subsidiary remain, and the acquisition procedure is scheduled to be completed in March next year.
This acquisition will be the largest global acquisition/merger (M&A) case since Posco International was integrated into the Posco Group last year.
Posco International decided to invest 50.1 percent and Hancock Energy with 49.9 percent, respectively.
Posco International said that demand for natural gas will continue to increase even during the energy transition era, and in the hydrogen market, blue hydrogen, which is based on natural gas, will divide the market with green hydrogen.
Posco International’s acquisition will also secure eighty-two billion cubic feet (802Bcf), equivalent to forty-four percent of South Korea’s natural gas consumption, as well as terrestrial gas field operations personnel in Australia.
