Three Gambling & Games in the "Kaiji" series that you can actually experience (Real Sound) - Yahoo! News
The gambling manga "Kaiji" series, which boasts explosive popularity mainly among men.
One of the real pleasures of this game is the extreme game with a life.
[Photo] Just by looking, my legs scoop up ... ... Challenge to cross the steel frame!
Therefore, this time, I would like to verify the game of Kaiji that can actually be played or practiced in the planning video.
■Numa It is a pachinko full of traps that appeared in "Gasting Hakairoku Kaiji".
In the original story, at a high rate of four thousand yen a ball, he stunned Kaiji.
In this swamp, there is a large trap of "nail forest", "movable character", and "three-stage cruin", and it was almost impossible to capture.
However, Kaiji used all kinds of hands, and at the end, he put a vinyl water tank in the building and went out of the rough work of sinking and tilting the ground, and captured it brilliantly.
"Numa", which appeared in Kaiji, actually appeared as a pachinko, and a lot of people are playing.
Of course, there is no such thing as "Ichidama 4000yen", and the difficulty has been lowered, but you will be able to taste the mood of Kaiji.
At the "Starside Party" held by the rich as an entertainer, it was carried out by the debtors, including Kaiji, to carry out the steel-frame crossing of "human horse racing".
The debtor proceeds while devising so that it does not fall over the thin steel frame installed ten meters above the ground and competes for its speed.
Twelve people participated, and the top twen can win prizes, but there are only four steel frames, and the safety measures are insufficient, and the possibility of dying is quite high.
This steel-frame crossing is highly dangerous, but it was developed as a VR game, and you can have an extremely close experience at "Eagle Bridge" installed at "Rakuten Life Park Miyagi", the home of professional baseball's Tohoku Rakuten Golden Eagles.
This eagle bridge is 20m high (equivalent to the 7th floor of the building), and there is "Sky Blanco" and "Victory One Bridge" at the end.
Of course, safety measures have been put in place.
Comedian Koala Koarashi released a video of him walking the Eagle Bridge on his YouTube, saying, "You can experience steel-marriing in Japan," and it became a hot topic.
E-card A two-player card game, "E-card".
They use one emperor's card, eight citizen's cards, and a total of ten slave cards, divided into the emperor's side and the slave side.
This game is made very well, and the emperor is strong against the citizens, the citizens are strong against the slaves, and the slaves are strong against the emperor.
Kaiji plays against Tonegawa under the strict rule that "if you lose, you can cut off your ears."
Kaiji realizes that a device that destroys the ear, such as earphones attached to the ears, is reading psychology by sensing and transmitting changes in the pulse and body temperature in the end, disrupting the Tone River by cutting his own ears to the limit and making the body an abnormal value.
E-cards are commercially available and can be purchased on Amazon.
On YouTube, popular YouTuber Hikaru uploaded a video of him playing the role of Kaiji in a movie with an e-card, which attracted a lot of attention.
■Do you want to taste Kaiji's mood?
I don't want everyone to be in a situation like Kaiji, but it's also true that when I read a manga, I can only taste the mood.
Through the game, you can feel the world view.
One step towards the new year, gently boosting Tora's big ema at Gokoku-jinja Shrine|Yamagata Shimbun
At the prefectural Gokoku-jinja Shrine (Yamagata City), where preparations for the new year are underway, next year's zodiac sign "Tora" large ema appeared.
On the 11th, students of the Tohoku University of Arts and Technology, who had designed it, visited the shrine and held a memorial service in front of the gods.
Since the year before last, the shrine has been asking for original paintings of ema from the University of the Arts.
This time, the work of Yui Tsuchiya (22), a third-year student, was drawn by nine members of the Nihonga Course in the Department of Fine Arts taught by Professor Toshiaki Suenaga.
The large ema is three and a half meters wide, and the height of the center is about one and a half meters.
Tsuchiya said that he drew "an image in which the cherry tree gently pushes the back of stepping into the new year".
The appearance of the tiger stopping and looking at the cherry blossoms included his wish, "Even in a rapidly changing world, I can afford to enjoy the beauty of nature."
Tsuchiya's design is also depicted in ema, which is generally distributed.
Kenichi Chiba, 44, of Gonnegi, said, "I think it will help all people overcome their difficulties."
