"Hakobune"'s "Fries of seasonal fish caught in the near sea and fried prawns homemade tartar sauce"|Life and Culture|Saga Shimbun News|Saga Shimbun LiVE
Bento "Frying seasonal fish caught in the near sea and fried shrimp homemade tartare sauce"
"hakobune" is a take-out specialty store with colorful bento boxes and deli (side dishes) made with plenty of vegetables.
Takayuki Kagetsu, 39, and Arumi, 38, opened the restaurant in August last year, saying, "I want people to feel like a restaurant at home."
One of the most popular bento's menus is "Frying seasonal fish caught in the sea and fried shrimp with homemade tartar sauce" (1000yen).
Fish choose the good things in the market from time to time.
"Fry is made as thin as possible so that you can understand the texture of the ingredients" (Mr. Takayuki), and you can directly understand the crispy texture of fried shrimp.
There are about four kinds of garnished vegetables and deli in the bento box, as well as mixed rice mixed with Hinohikari produced in Saga Prefecture, rice with small grains, and soup.
Vegetables are sourced from homemade buckwheat fields and purchased at a direct shop in the prefecture.
Side dishes change depending on the time of year, but Mr. Takayuki is trained in French cuisine, and lapes and rata teuilles add color.
On the other hand, it is a fusion of Japanese and Western styles that can be enjoyed by a wide range of generations, such as "a relaxing taste that you are accustomed to eating" like dashi rolled eggs.
The bento "Domestic-aligned meat hand-made hamburger steak" (1000yen) is also popular.
From next year, we will also release "Charcutery Set", a processed meat product that goes well with wine and alcohol.
