The future of inheritance and gift tax "revision" that makes the gift of the lifetime "forbidden hand", Amari Akira, the former chairman of the LDP's taste!
"Weekly Diamond" The first feature of the December 18th issue says, "Talk with your family during the year-end and New Year holidays!
It’s a gift and an inheritance.”
In the midst of the discussion of the integration of inheritance tax and the gift tax, it was postponed in the tax reform outline of FY2022, but in the near future, there is a great possibility that lifetime gifts, which is the royal road of inheritance tax measures, will become a "prohibited hand".
How will the rules of inheritance change?
In addition to a direct hit on the former chairman of the LDP's Tax Conditioner and Mr. Akira Amari of the People's House of Representatives, we will teach them everything from the basics of gifting and inheritance to tax-saving techniques, which will be made in time for the next year.
(Diamond Editorial Department, Hiroaki Miyahara )
"From the point of view of inheritance tax and the gift tax in a more integrated manner, we will proceed with a full-scale examination toward the establishment of a tax system that is neutral on the choice of the timing of asset transfer."
In a statement released last year by the ruling party on the outline of the FY2021 tax reform, a major upheaval has spread not only to wealthy people but also to the middle class.
This is because it means to change the rules of inheritance completely, and to raise the inheritance tax by making "lifetime gifts", which is the royal road of inheritance tax measures, a "prohibited hand".
The iron rules for advanced inheritance tax protection measures are to "reduce the amount of property subject to taxation."
The most powerful trump card, lifetime gifts, have been widely used not only by wealthy people, but also by company employees who have a small inheritance tax due to having a home in the three major metropolitan areas.
In the midst of this, the discussion of "the integration of inheritance tax and the gift tax".
Although it was postponed by the FY22 tax reform outline announced on December 10th, when it had been concerned about the introduction of the fastest, a policy for integration was once again hammered out with more in-depth language, such as “We will review the current inheritance settlement taxation system and the way of the calendar-year gift system” and “Since the tax-exempt measures of the gift tax do not ask for any tax burden on the transfer of assets within the family within the limit within the limit ...
In an interview with this editorial department, former Liberal Democratic Party (LDP), former chairman of the tax investigation and former Secretary General Akira Amari said.
"The most important thing is to lose the advantages and disadvantages due to the timing of property transfer, and to make the tax burden the same at any time.
At the moment, we are simulating what kind of problems will come out (due to integration).
Even so, in the near future, there is no doubt that there will be a big cut in the direction of invalidating lifetime gifts as a tax-saving measure.
So, how will the rules of inheritance and gift taxes change?
