South Korea's Samsung Electronics Establishes "DX Division" that integrates Home Appliances and Mobile, Emphasizing User Experience (WoW!Korea) - Yahoo! News
Following the integration of the CE and IM divisions as a set division, Samsung Electronics announced on the 12th that it has decided on the name DX (Device eXperience) and will reflect this in the year-end reorganization.
Through a variety of services, from mobile to home appliances, it can be read that the intention is to enhance user experience.
Samsung Electronics announced that the newly launched DX division by integrating the CE and IM divisions consists of divisions such as VD (Visual Display), household appliances, medical devices, MX (Mobile eXperience) and networks.
A Samsung Electronics official said, "This name change reflects the medium- to long-term business structure, future-orientedness, and the strengthening of global leadership."
In addition to products such as TVs, home appliances, smartphones, and communication facilities, he emphasized the intention to make it easy for consumers to enjoy optimized experiences through services and solutions that reflect the needs of customers.
With the establishment of an integrated leadership system, the strategy of creating synergies across organizations and building a foundation for products and services that are differentiated on a company-wide scale was also reflected in the name.
Already, Samsung Electronics is envisioning a strategy to make content and services freely available to users through interlocking devices, such as home appliances and smartphones based on the Internet of Things (IoT) and artificial intelligence (AI), through the Multi-Device Experience (MDE) Council.
