Twenty-four cars collided, the trailer driver does not have a chronic illness Is it carelessness (Television Asahi (ANN)) - Yahoo! News
Twenty-four cars collided in Komaki City, Aichi Prefecture, and it was found that the driver of the trailer who was arrested and arrested did not have a chronic illness, and it seems that the accident occurred due to some inattention.
On the morning of the 10th, twenty-four trucks and passenger cars collided on the 41st national highway in Komaki City, and twelve people were lightly injured.
The police arrested 54-year-old Katsuya Nomura, who was driving the trailer, on charges of causing injury to a 71-year-old man and causing injury to a 71-year-old man in the first crash, and was arrested on Monday morning.
Even after the accident, Nomura's trailer continued to proceed without stepping on the brakes, and the fire department also confirmed that Nomura temporarily lost consciousness immediately after the accident.
However, according to investigators, it was found that Nomura did not have a chronic illness, and it seems that it was caused by some inattention.
The police are looking into the situation at the time.
