●"Kinnikuman" volume4 review contributor name Oginuma X★★★★★★ (five out of five stars) ● Superhuman professional wrestling has already started before the game!
In a word, this four-volume is a book that carefully and carefully depicts the final match of Kinnikuman versus Robin mask, but the first thing I want to keep in mind is that it is not a volume that depicts only the match on the ring.
Starting from the signing ceremony, it is difficult to go to the game, such as each other's restrainting battle and special training scenery, but it is never boring.
This feeling in the work, in which the tension that the first battle of the century is about to begin is gradually increasing, and it is surely connected to the rise of the reader's tension, and I am impressed that even this period is a really calculated production.
And one more mountain before the important final, what you can't miss is the 3rd place decision match between Terry Man and Ramen Man.
In addition to the gorgeousness as a competitive card, what I like is that behind the scenes before the game, the ramen man pointed to Kinnikuman's poster "It's my turn from now on!"
Trying to beat the chop.
However, Terryman who happened to pass by accepted the sword and stopped it, stared silently at each other, and it was a scene in which it just separated by itself.
What’s amazing about this is that both of them have already been defeated, and there is no longer an opportunity to fight Kinnikuman in this tournament.
However, there is such a thing as 悶肶もん wearing about that kinnikuman.
If you can show me like this, I can't help but think about the activities of the distant future!
That's what it's like for a character to stand, and it's a scene that still makes me keen as a manga artist!
The battle between the two of them ends without cutting the length, but the famous scene complains about the tears of the ramen man after the game.
I said to Kinnikuman, “Don’t be afraid of God’s luck!”
It's a line.
I think that this is a grand meta statement on the work itself, and until now, I think that the reader also felt that Kinnikuman does not lose because it is the main character after all, and that it is somehow winning in a place where it is not the ability.
However, by letting the ramen man make this statement, Mr. Boiled Tamago stepped ahead and couldn't use his hands anymore.
In one word, the reader said, "Well then, Kinnikuman will defeat Robin with his ability?
How?" "
If you look at it from another artist's point of view, you can imagine it again in an unpredictable development, and from another writer's point of view, it is a line that the boiled egg teacher who makes the work imposes restrictions on himself.
I think this has done something amazing.
I think it’s definitely one of the most important aspects of this series.
