The number of people infected with the new coronavirus in the military has increased to thirty ... all breakthrough infections = South Korea (WoW! Korea) - Yahoo! News
On the 12th, the number of people infected with the new coronavirus in the South Korean army increased by thirty from the previous day.
All of the new infections were breakthrough cases.
South Korea's Ministry of Defense announced that the cumulative number of new coronavirus cases in the military on a 2pm basis on the same day increased from the previous day to 2713.
Sixteen people were in the Army, but were tallied with six members of the Navy, six members of the Air Force, and two other units.
Of the cumulative infections, the number of patients currently undergoing treatment and management has increased to 977.
Thirty-three breakthrough cases were reported the day before.
